DECISION CliDoesTheMechanicalWorkAgentsOnlyJudge
	TITLE "every mechanical step of a wave is a CLI command; a model is called only to judge"
	STATUS active
	DESC "branches, worktrees, ordering, launching, polling, merging, rebasing, statistics, report"
		+ "skeletons and signal normalisation are deterministic code of the CLI; an agent receives"
		+ "a pre-computed context from one command and returns a verdict or a text through another"
	REJECTED "a coordinator agent that orchestrates the wave: it rediscovers state at every step"
		+ "and spends judgment on bookkeeping"
	REJECTED "letting each run read git, gh and files itself: measured, the first edit of a task"
		+ "run came after 23 steps and 134 000 tokens in median"
	RATIONALE "the user's first principle for the plan; the measured cost of discovery is the"
		+ "largest saving available"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 1 and 5"

DECISION TheToolIsNamedBrigade
	TITLE "the CLI, the repository and the config directory are named brigade"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the kitchen brigade is the team of roles under the chef, who is the user; the"
		+ "verification gate is nicknamed the pass"
	REJECTED "fab: collides with the Fabric CLI"
	REJECTED "chef, kitchen: collide with the Chef ecosystem's CLIs"
	REJECTED "expo, pass: collide with the Expo CLI and the pass password store"
	RATIONALE "free on PATH and in Debian packages on 2026-10-04; the metaphor is the one the user"
		+ "adopted from the talk"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 3"

DECISION PythonStandardLibraryOnly
	TITLE "brigade is Python 3.11 or later, standard library only, with POSIX sh only in the"
		+ "optional scheduler files; no third-party dependency"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "a Bun or TypeScript CLI: ties a machine-wide tool to a JavaScript toolchain the"
		+ "instructions corpus does not have"
	REJECTED "a TUI framework: a new dependency for views the web dashboard renders"
	RATIONALE "the hooks, the unattended runner and the user's local context page are already"
		+ "Python and sh; 3.11 is the floor tomllib needs and nothing in the plan needs a later"
		+ "feature"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 15 and 16"

DECISION ADeterministicTickReplacesTheCoordinatorAgent
	TITLE "the coordinator is brigade tick, a deterministic pass run every five minutes by the"
		+ "machine's scheduler: the user systemd timer where a user instance runs, else a cron line"
		+ "or brigade tick --loop"
	STATUS active
	DESC "it reconciles waves with git and GitHub, advances task states, launches runs within the"
		+ "slot cap, merges verified pull requests and records events"
	REJECTED "a long-lived coordinator session: costs tokens for waiting and loses state at"
		+ "compaction"
	REJECTED "cloud routines: private data and the worktrees are on the machine only"
	RATIONALE "every transition is a condition evaluated from facts; the laptop being off loses"
		+ "nothing, the next tick after boot resumes"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 5 and 17"

DECISION HybridStorageCorpusAndLedger
	TITLE "durable facts live in awawa corpora, high-volume events in an append-only JSONL ledger"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the brigade corpus holds PROJECT, POLICY, STUDY, ORDER, REQUEST, PATTERN and CONSTRAINT;"
		+ "each project corpus keeps its WAVE and TASK entities; the ledger holds runs, states,"
		+ "pauses and merges"
	REJECTED "everything in awawa: one entity per run means thousands of entities and git noise"
	REJECTED "SQLite for everything: a second grammar without schema lint"
	RATIONALE "the user's answer to the storage question; one home per fact, views rendered never"
		+ "hand-maintained"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 13 and 14"

DECISION AVerifierRunOnEveryPullRequestAndOneHumanGate
	TITLE "every pull request passes a deterministic preflight then one prudence run before merging"
		+ "into integration; the user merges integration into main"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "the user reviewing every diff: the rung the user asked to leave"
	REJECTED "sampling that blocks: sampling stays a suggestion in the report"
	RATIONALE "the user's answers on autonomy and review; delivered work is never verified by the"
		+ "run that produced it"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 7"

DECISION QuotaPausesTheWaveAndResumesTheSameSession
	TITLE "a rate-limit result pauses the wave; the resume is the adapter's resume of the suspended"
		+ "session at the time the message names, or a fresh launch from the progress file when the"
		+ "adapter has no resume"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "a dollar cap: the subscription is the cap"
	REJECTED "probing the quota with extra calls: the resume itself is the probe"
	REJECTED "treating a client without resume as unsupported: the progress file is the contract"
		+ "every run already keeps"
	RATIONALE "the user's answer on budget: waves of 10 to 20 pull requests, the quota blocks"
		+ "before any overspend"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 17"

DECISION TheDashboardIsBuiltThePluginAndAwawaWebAreKept
	TITLE "a loopback web dashboard is built; the IntelliJ plugin stays for in-IDE work; awawa-web"
		+ "stays the editor of the brigade corpus"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the dashboard exposes a local JSON API the plugin may consume later for a branch selector"
	REJECTED "extending the plugin into the factory's UI: it would have to grow a server and a"
		+ "ledger reader of its own"
	REJECTED "a second corpus editor in the dashboard: awawa-web already edits block by block with"
		+ "fmt and lint"
	RATIONALE "the plugin's handbook names user-defined views as its extension point; the branch"
		+ "selector is a server-side fact (git archive per SHA)"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 15"

DECISION AwawaIsWrappedAsItIs
	TITLE "the plan wraps the awawa binary as it is; desired changes go to a list of requests to"
		+ "its author, never on the critical path"
	STATUS active
	REJECTED "forking awawa or waiting for a feature: the user is a consumer and the author may"
		+ "lack time"
	RATIONALE "every awawa gap has a workaround the POC uses: block edits with fmt and lint,"
		+ "per-entity spawns cached per SHA"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 19"

DECISION MinedConstraintsAreDeliveredAsWaves
	TITLE "constraints mined from transcripts become waves like any other work, auto-merged into"
		+ "integration and listed in the report with their reason"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the scrubber runs inside the transcript collectors before anything is written, on the"
		+ "PRIVATE patterns of each registered project and on brigade's built-ins, e-mail addresses"
		+ "and home paths; a set computed at run time is never stored"
	REJECTED "proposals only in the dashboard: the user asked for the same autonomy as a wave"
	REJECTED "a stored list of real names for the scrubber: no correspondence between a real name"
		+ "and a pseudonym is kept anywhere"
	RATIONALE "the user's answer on mining; no real identifier leaves the machine"
	SOURCE "the Artifact Brigade Blueprint, plan section 12"

DECISION TheCorpusIsTheHomeOfTaskStatusTheBoardItsView
	TITLE "the corpus is the single home of task status; the task board of the Artifact is a view"
		+ "of it"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a task's STATUS is edited in docs/tasks.awawa and nowhere else"
	DESC "the board of the Blueprint shows the status the corpus holds, written by a deterministic"
		+ "command"
	DESC "a status changed on the board binds nothing"
	REJECTED "the board as the home of status until the brigade delivers its own waves, the"
		+ "planning run's choice: the corpus held every task draft while the board showed them"
		+ "todo, two homes already disagreeing"
	REJECTED "two homes kept in sync by hand: a hand-maintained view is wrong by the next commit"
	RATIONALE "the plan's own principle, one home per fact, views rendered never hand-maintained;"
		+ "ruled by the user on 2026-10-05"
	SOURCE "pull request #1 of the brigade repository"

DECISION BrigadeNamesNoAiClientOutsideItsAdapters
	TITLE "brigade's core names no AI client: every launch, result, resume, transcript read and"
		+ "tool grant goes through a client adapter, and each capability a client lacks has a"
		+ "recorded fallback"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a client adapter answers five operations as JSON documents, probe, launch, result, resume"
		+ "and transcripts; it is a built-in module or an executable brigade-client-<name> on PATH"
	DESC "probe declares the optional operations the client supports; the core applies the fallback"
		+ "of each missing one: no resume, a fresh launch from the progress file; no step count,"
		+ "steps null and the budget held on wall time; no transcripts, brigade's own run logs; no"
		+ "per-tool grant, the client's unattended mode and a disposable worktree for a reading"
		+ "slot; no reset hour in a rate-limit message, now plus thirty minutes"
	DESC "the core spawns the process itself, in the worktree, with the brief, the role package,"
		+ "the capabilities and the budget the adapter translated; the ledger wraps every client"
		+ "the same way"
	DESC "worktrees are git's, never the client's; background sessions of a client are not used"
	DESC "the README lists the supported clients and, for each adapter operation, the support"
		+ "level, full, fallback or absent, generated from the probe declarations; a test fails"
		+ "when the table drifts"
	DESC "the Claude Code adapter is the first; the sandbox rehearsal runs on every installed"
		+ "adapter and on the fake adapter the test suite launches"
	REJECTED "brigade as hooks, commands and agent files of one CLI: unusable with another client,"
		+ "and the instructions corpus already rules its own files agent-agnostic"
	REJECTED "an SDK per client: a third-party dependency each, where the command line of a client"
		+ "is the contract its vendor documents"
	REJECTED "refusing a client that lacks resume or per-tool grants: each fallback above costs"
		+ "nothing a wave cannot absorb"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled on 2026-10-05 that brigade presupposes neither Claude Code nor its"
		+ "workings and that the README names the supported tools with their level; four clients"
		+ "document a non-interactive mode with a JSON output (Claude Code 2.1.289 --help, Codex"
		+ "exec, OpenCode run, Gemini headless, read on 2026-10-05) and only Claude Code is"
		+ "installed on the reference machine"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"

DECISION RolesAreSlotsBoundToRoleFiles
	TITLE "a procedure calls a slot, never a role name; a role is a Markdown file with a flat front"
		+ "matter and a system prompt body; a slot resolves to a role in a fixed order ending on"
		+ "brigade's built-in roles"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the slots are plan, build, verify, review, rebase, report, triage, rules and explore"
	DESC "a role file declares name, slot, reasoning (deepest, deep, standard, light), capabilities"
		+ "(read, write, shell, net), budget and returns; its body is the whole system prompt of"
		+ "the run"
	DESC "a slot resolves in this order: a PROJECT.ROLE override, the machine's roles directory,"
		+ "the AGENT entities of the instructions corpus when config names one, brigade's built-in"
		+ "roles"
	DESC "an AGENT entity is read through awawa --json at launch time: WORK, REASONING, CAPABILITY,"
		+ "BUDGET and RETURNS fill the front matter, its context package is the body"
	DESC "the reasoning level maps to a model and an effort in the client adapter's table,"
		+ "overridable in the machine config; a role file never names a model"
	DESC "brigade ships a built-in role for every slot: ada plans, bilal reports, mina triages, and"
		+ "one builder, verifier, reviewer, rebaser, rule writer and explorer"
	REJECTED "roles living only in the instructions corpus: presupposes that corpus on every"
		+ "machine"
	REJECTED "roles written in one client's agent-file format: bound to that client"
	REJECTED "a model name in a role file: the depth is the role's and the model the adapter's, as"
		+ "the AGENT schema of the instructions corpus already states"
	RATIONALE "the user asked on 2026-10-05 for custom roles and for their own roles by default,"
		+ "and named the reporter bilal; @SCHEMA.AGENT of the instructions corpus separates"
		+ "REASONING from the model each adapter binds"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"

DECISION BrigadeInstallsFromOneFileWithFourPrerequisites
	TITLE "brigade installs on any Linux from one zipapp or a clone; Python 3.11 or later, git,"
		+ "awawa and one adapted AI client are the prerequisites; the scheduler, the forge account,"
		+ "the instructions corpus and the IDE tools are optional"
	STATUS active
	DESC "brigade doctor checks Python 3.11 or later, git, awawa 2.7 or later and the configured"
		+ "client adapter's probe, and reports each optional item with its fallback as a warning,"
		+ "never a finding"
	DESC "optional with its fallback: a user systemd instance, else a cron line or brigade tick"
		+ "--loop; gh with the machine account, else the user's gh account recorded in the ledger"
		+ "on every write, else local mode without a forge; the instructions corpus, else built-in"
		+ "roles and no instructions package; awawa-web and the IDE plugin, dashboard only"
	DESC "machine bindings live in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/brigade/config.toml: client, scheduler, forge"
		+ "account, instructions corpus root, the reasoning-to-model table, the IDE link; ratified"
		+ "facts stay in the corpus"
	DESC "custom roles, collectors, checks and recipes live under $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/brigade/ in"
		+ "roles/, collectors/, checks/ and recipes/; state in $XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/; the refs"
		+ "and collector caches in $XDG_CACHE_HOME/brigade/"
	DESC "the repository builds dist/brigade.pyz with the standard zipapp module; the file runs"
		+ "with python3 alone"
	REJECTED "pip or pipx: absent from the reference Debian 13 (command -v pip pipx, 2026-10-05)"
	REJECTED "systemd as a prerequisite: the tick is one command any scheduler runs"
	REJECTED "machine bindings as corpus entities: a probed capability is not a ratified fact, and"
		+ "the corpus is a git history"
	RATIONALE "the user ruled on 2026-10-05 that brigade installs and runs on another Linux machine"
		+ "with another AI client"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"

DECISION ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles
	TITLE "the command line with --json is the contract, state lives in language-neutral files and"
		+ "black-box CLI tests are the acceptance suite, so that a port to another language is a"
		+ "port and not a redesign"
	STATUS active
	DESC "every command prints --json with stable field names and the documented exit codes; the"
		+ "dashboard, the agents and the tests use the command line, never the package"
	DESC "state is JSONL, JSON, TOML, Markdown with a flat front matter and awawa corpora; recipes"
		+ "are TOML; no pickle, shelve or private database; a sqlite file may only be a derived"
		+ "cache deletable at any time"
	DESC "every result, event, collector, recipe and config document carries a schema version"
	DESC "tests/cli drives brigade as a subprocess against fixtures, a sandbox git repository, the"
		+ "fake client adapter and recorded forge answers; a port passes this suite before"
		+ "replacing the Python"
	DESC "the client, forge and scheduler adapters, the collectors, the checks and the outputs are"
		+ "process-shaped boundaries: a built-in one is a module, an external one an executable on"
		+ "PATH, both answering the same JSON documents"
	DESC "the core never imports an adapter module; a guard script under tests checks the import"
		+ "graph"
	DESC "the language of the distributed version is decided at M3 with the ledger's measures, Go"
		+ "or Rust"
	REJECTED "a Rust rewrite now: no toolchain on the reference machine (command -v rustc cargo,"
		+ "2026-10-05), every crate a dependency the standard-library ruling refuses, and the"
		+ "tool's shape still open"
	REJECTED "a Go rewrite now: the same absent toolchain; Go stays the target that keeps a"
		+ "standard-library-only policy with a static binary"
	REJECTED "PyInstaller or Nuitka: third-party packagers for what zipapp does"
	RATIONALE "the user asked on 2026-10-05 for an architecture that eases a later migration to"
		+ "Rust or another distributable form; what these rules keep outside the Python package is"
		+ "what a port carries over unchanged"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"

DECISION AStudyIsDeterministicCollectorsThenOneJudgingRun
	TITLE "work that is not a wave, a report, a data collection, an audit, a research, is a study:"
		+ "declared deterministic collectors assemble the evidence, then at most one judging run"
		+ "answers from that evidence alone and returns through brigade study answer"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a STUDY entity of the brigade corpus holds the question verbatim, the project when there"
		+ "is one, the collectors, the judging slot or none, the schedule or none, the output and"
		+ "an optional template"
	DESC "a collector is a declared executable or built-in that prints one JSON document, run by"
		+ "the CLI with the study's parameters in its environment, cached by the hash of its"
		+ "command and inputs, never a model"
	DESC "collectors resolve in order: the project's .brigade/collectors/, the machine's collectors"
		+ "directory, brigade-collector-<name> on PATH, brigade's built-ins; the shell collector"
		+ "runs a command line declared in the study"
	DESC "brigade study context prints the question, each collector's summary with the path of its"
		+ "full document, the template's skeleton filled with the collected values and the expected"
		+ "shape of the answer; the judging run reads nothing a collector already collected"
	DESC "brigade study answer validates the answer, refuses one that changed a CLI-filled section"
		+ "of the skeleton, writes it to the declared output, inbox signal, file on a branch,"
		+ "corpus entity or forge issue, and records the ledger event; an executable"
		+ "brigade-output-<name> on PATH adds an output"
	DESC "the report slot answers with a narrative, the explore slot with findings and their"
		+ "evidence, the triage slot with patterns, the rules slot with rules"
	DESC "a study with no judging slot is a scan: its non-empty output is the answer; the gardening"
		+ "scans of M4 declare OUTPUT inbox"
	DESC "the wave report, the triage and the miner are the built-in studies wave-report, triage"
		+ "and mine-transcripts"
	DESC "a study runs on demand with brigade study run, or when due, by the tick, under the slot"
		+ "cap; a study that needs a second judgment is two studies, the second reading the first's"
		+ "answer through the study collector"
	DESC "study is the built-in recipe study, its ordered steps collect, judge and output written"
		+ "under the recipe engine's contract; its collect steps come from the STUDY entity's"
		+ "COLLECTOR lines"
	REJECTED "a judging run that collects by itself: the two explorer runs the user saw spent"
		+ "judgment on collection, the measured cost of discovery"
	REJECTED "one entity per kind, routine, report, triage, miner: four schedulers, four context"
		+ "builders and four answer writers for one shape"
	REJECTED "collectors as Python modules only: a port would carry them, where an executable"
		+ "printing JSON is the same contract in any language"
	RATIONALE "the user asked on 2026-10-05 whether brigade separates judgment from mechanics for"
		+ "work that is not a wave; the first principle applies to every kind of work, and the"
		+ "miner of the plan already had this shape for one case"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"

DECISION AKindOfWorkIsARecipeAnInstanceAnOrder
	TITLE "a user declares a new kind of work as a recipe, a TOML file of ordered process-shaped"
		+ "steps run by one engine of the tick; an order is one instance of a recipe; wave stays"
		+ "native and study is the first built-in recipe"
	STATUS active
	DESC "a recipe declares schema, name, description, params, max_wall and ordered steps of the"
		+ "kinds collect, command, gate, judge, output, order, corpus and op, op being worktree,"
		+ "commit, pull-request or merge through the adapters; a value substitutes {param} from the"
		+ "order and the project, nothing else: no expression, no loop, no fan-out"
	DESC "a judge step names a slot, a procedure and the shape of its answer; it receives only the"
		+ "run directory's documents through brigade order context, answers through brigade order"
		+ "answer, and is a run with its procedure's budget, counted in the slot cap and recorded"
		+ "in the ledger"
	DESC "a gate step names a check, an executable printing ok and reason, resolved like a"
		+ "collector; a failed gate or command parks the order with the step's reason unless the"
		+ "recipe says skip, stop or retry:N; nothing is assumed, and a parked order resumes once"
		+ "the user acted"
	DESC "each step's result is a file under the run directory; a resumed order restarts at its"
		+ "first undone step; the ledger holds order.started, step.done, step.failed, order.parked"
		+ "and order.done"
	DESC "recipes resolve in order: the project's .brigade/recipes/, the machine's recipes"
		+ "directory, brigade's recipes/; brigade recipe lint checks the schema, that every"
		+ "collector, check, output, procedure and slot resolves, that every param is declared, and"
		+ "refuses a client or model key"
	DESC "an ORDER entity of the brigade corpus holds the recipe, the project, the user's words,"
		+ "the parameters, the schedule and the output; a REQUEST is the order of the native recipe"
		+ "wave, a STUDY the order of the recipe study; a recipe places a wave or another order"
		+ "through an order step"
	DESC "the engine arrives in M8, once wave and study exist: study is written in M1 as ordered"
		+ "steps under the engine's contract, so the engine replaces its orchestration without a"
		+ "command changing"
	REJECTED "a workflow language with expressions, loops and fan-out: a second language to lint,"
		+ "and the wave's scheduling, the one lifecycle that needs loops and fan-out, is exact code"
		+ "whose savings the plan measures"
	REJECTED "the wave as a declared recipe: fan-out per task, repair loops with caps, the overlap"
		+ "order and the quota pause are code; a recipe places a wave order instead"
	REJECTED "recipes as corpus entities: a recipe is nested and code-like, versioned with the"
		+ "project it serves; the corpus keeps the orders, which are facts"
	REJECTED "the engine in M1: until a second recipe exists it would generalise one case; the"
		+ "contract is fixed in M1 and the engine built in M8"
	REJECTED "the names workflow, playbook, procedure and routine: the first is the vocabulary of"
		+ "the continuous integration the pass reads check runs from, the second another tool's"
		+ "term outside the kitchen, the third the portable file a judging step runs, the fourth"
		+ "the name just merged into study"
	RATIONALE "the user asked on 2026-10-05 for a way to add kinds of work on demand and proposed"
		+ "the word recipe; the user's own usage-report command, 21 000 characters bound to one"
		+ "client, is the first recipe to write: three collectors, one gate, one judging run, one"
		+ "file on the pull request's branch"
	SOURCE "pull request #3 of the brigade repository"

DECISION TheBlueprintIsADevelopmentArtefactRetiredByTheDashboard
	TITLE "the Blueprint Artifact is an artefact of brigade's development phase, retired when the"
		+ "dashboard shows the corpus's tasks"
	STATUS active
	DESC "the Blueprint Artifact, plan, mockups, demo and task board, lives for the development of"
		+ "brigade and no longer"
	DESC "it is retired when the Corpus view of the dashboard (M3) shows every task of the brigade"
		+ "corpus with its status; the board is then republished no more"
	DESC "until then the board is a view of docs/tasks.awawa, refreshed from awawa status TASK at"
		+ "each republication of the Artifact, never by hand"
	DESC "at retirement the plan is frozen as a dated document, readable, never rewritten; a SOURCE"
		+ "naming a section of the plan reads the frozen plan"
	DESC "the board page carries no automated test; it is checked by viewing the published page"
	REJECTED "regular-expression tests of the page source, the tests of pull request #5: they test"
		+ "how the code is written, not what the page shows, for a page that will be retired"
	REJECTED "a JavaScript test runtime for the page: a runtime adopted for a page that will be"
		+ "retired"
	REJECTED "a sync command of brigade writing the corpus's statuses to the board, B41 of pull"
		+ "request #4: a command written for a page that will be retired, when a republication"
		+ "refreshes the view"
	REJECTED "deleting the plan at retirement: the decisions cite its sections as SOURCE"
	RATIONALE "ruled by the user on 2026-10-05: the Blueprint has no life beyond the implementation"
		+ "of brigade, its board is superseded by the dashboard brigade serves itself, and its plan"
		+ "becomes a dated document once brigade exists; the same day the tests of the board page"
		+ "were ruled to test the wrong thing, the page being proven by looking at it"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-05, pull request #6 of the brigade repository"
